    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/yasher3413/twig/tarball/v0.1.2",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/yasher3413/twig/zipball/v0.1.2",
    "body": "**[Download twig-macos-arm64.dmg](https://github.com/yasher3413/twig/releases/download/v0.1.2/twig-macos-arm64.dmg)**. Requires a Mac with an Apple chip (M1 or newer).\n\n### New\n- **Report a bug from inside twig.** Help → Report a Bug…, ⌘K \"Report a bug\", or Settings → Browser. Describe what happened and twig files it as a GitHub issue for you. It only sends what you write, plus twig and macOS versions if you leave that ticked. It never sends the page you're on or your history.\n\n### Fixed\n- **Gmail no longer says the browser isn't supported.** twig was telling sites it was an old Safari; it now reports the Safari version your Mac actually has.\n- **Address bar autofill stays highlighted as you keep typing**, like Chrome, so your next letter replaces the suggestion instead of landing after it.\n- **Only one twig in Spotlight.** A copy left over from building the app no longer shows up next to the installed one.\n\n### First launch\ntwig isn't notarized by Apple yet. The first time you open it, macOS says it can't verify the app. Go to **System Settings → Privacy & Security** and click **Open Anyway**.\n"
