    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/yasher3413/twig/tarball/v0.1.1",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/yasher3413/twig/zipball/v0.1.1",
    "body": "**[Download twig-macos-arm64.dmg](https://github.com/yasher3413/twig/releases/download/v0.1.1/twig-macos-arm64.dmg)**. Requires a Mac with an Apple chip (M1 or newer).\n\n### New\n- **Use twig as your default browser.** Go to Settings → Browser → *Make twig your default browser*. Links you click in other apps then open as a new tab in your current space.\n\n### Fixed\n- Tabs show the page's own title (\"Leafs – Google Search\", \"GitHub\") instead of just the site's address.\n- Tabs show each site's icon, dimmed while the tab is asleep.\n- Websites follow twig's theme: set twig to Dark and pages that support dark mode go dark too.\n- Address bar autofill completes to sites (`g` → `google.com`) instead of old search results. History now includes the pages you click through to, not only ones you type. Clicking into the address bar selects the whole address.\n- Embedded frames (ads, videos, hidden frames) no longer overwrite a tab's address.\n- The first letter you type after ⌘K no longer goes missing.\n- The active tab curves smoothly into the toolbar, with no stray corners.\n- The new tab page's shortcuts sit together instead of spreading down the page.\n\n### First launch\ntwig isn't notarized by Apple yet. The first time you open it, macOS says it can't verify the app. Go to **System Settings → Privacy & Security** and click **Open Anyway**.\n"
