    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/yasher3413/twig/zipball/v0.1.0",
    "body": "The first release of twig: a Mac browser that lets you keep your tabs.\n\n**[Download twig-macos-arm64.dmg](https://github.com/yasher3413/twig/releases/download/v0.1.0/twig-macos-arm64.dmg)**. Requires a Mac with an Apple chip (M1 or newer).\n\n### What's in it\n- **Sleeping tabs:** tabs you aren't looking at hibernate and cost almost nothing. Only a few stay awake.\n- **Recall (⇧⌘F):** search the text of pages you've actually read, stored only on your Mac.\n- **Changes since you last read:** revisit a page and twig shows what changed in its text.\n- **Snooze and sweep (⌥⌘S):** snooze a tab until later, and archive tabs you haven't touched in weeks when twig suggests it.\n- **Spaces and checkpoints:** separate sets of tabs, with saved snapshots you can return to or fork.\n- **Research packages (⇧⌘P):** export and import a space with its notes and excerpts.\n- **⌘K command palette**, a reader view, link hints (⌘E), bookmarks and history, downloads, per-site zoom, private windows, and rebindable shortcuts.\n\n### First launch\ntwig isn't notarized by Apple yet. The first time you open it, macOS says it can't verify the app. Go to **System Settings → Privacy & Security** and click **Open Anyway**. After that it opens normally.\n"
